## From Type to Iterator

```xiom
pub interface IntoIterator {
  type Item;
  type IntoIter: Iterator[Item = Self::Item];
  fn into_iter(self: Self) -> Self::IntoIter;
}
```

### How for..in Works
```xiom
for item in collection {
  // use item
}

// Desugars to:
let mut iter = collection.into_iter();
while let Some(item) = iter.next() {
  // use item
}
```

### Implementing IntoIterator
```xiom
pub type MyList[T] = Vec[T];

impl IntoIterator for MyList[T] {
  type Item = T;
  type IntoIter = VecIter[T];

  fn into_iter(self: MyList[T]) -> VecIter[T] {
    return MyList[T].iter();
  }
}

// Now you can write:
let list = MyList[Int]();
list.push(1); list.push(2); list.push(3);
for item in list {
  io.println(item.to_str());  // 1, 2, 3
}
```

### IntoIterator vs Iterator
```
IntoIterator: "I can BECOME an iterator"
Iterator:     "I AM an iterator"

for..in uses IntoIterator
.chain(), .map() use Iterator
```

### Three Forms of Iteration
```xiom
for item in &collection { }   // Borrow each element (IntoIterator for &Type)
for item in &mut collection { } // Mutable borrow
for item in collection { }      // Consume the collection (IntoIterator for Type)
```

